Sync first pulls Backend changes for tracked open Items, then applies queued
Mutations in order. Unresolved title/body edits protect those fields from
Pull, and an unresolved Priority or Effort change protects that field; other
Shared Fields can still refresh. Sync requires a configured Remote.
.PP
Pull also brings in the Backend's Dependencies between Items bound to it: it
adds the ones the Backend lists and removes the ones it no longer does, except
an edge an unresolved block or unblock still protects. Pull ignores a blocker
with no bound Item, and skips an edge that would make an Item wait on itself,
with a warning on stderr.
.PP
Pull also brings in each Ticket's parent when that parent is an Item bound
to the Backend: it replaces the Ticket's Container, even a Local one, and
clears a bound Container the Backend no longer lists. An unresolved parent
change protects the Ticket's Container. A Local Container stays while the
Backend lists no bound parent. Pull skips a parent tk cannot nest or that
would make an Item wait on itself, with a warning on stderr; the Ticket then
keeps a Local Container but loses a bound one.
.PP
A failed Mutation stops later Mutations from applying. Inspect it with
.B tk sync log
and retry sync after fixing the cause. Use
.B \-\-skip
to give up a failed non-Promotion Mutation; the skip commits before Backend
access. An indeterminate Promotion is not replayed automatically: use
.BR "tk promote reconcile" ,
.BR "tk promote retry" ,
or
.BR "tk promote cancel" .
